# Use the subclass mock maker instead of Mockito's default inline mock maker.
#
# The inline mock maker instruments loaded classes via a Java agent that it
# self-attaches at runtime by spawning an external process. That attach is
# blocked in sandboxed and hardened environments, and when it fails Mockito
# reports it as "unable to load the default implementation of MockMaker", which
# aborts every @SpringBootTest before the first assertion -- even in tests that
# use no mocks at all, because Spring Boot's ResetMocksTestExecutionListener
# initializes Mockito unconditionally.
#
# The subclass mock maker needs no agent. Its only limitation is that it cannot
# mock final classes, final methods or statics. Nothing in this project's tests
# does: the seams that get mocked are interfaces (the Gmail transport, the
# clock), which is the design the ingestion framework was built around anyway.
mock-maker-subclass
